  - "Ask a seven-year-old to sit still and describe their anxiety and you will probably get a shrug. Hand that same child a bucket, a patch of wet sand, and an hour beside the water, and you will hear the whole thing: who the castle belongs to, who is allowed inside, what happens when the tide comes. Sand Castle Therapy™ is a nature-based play therapy model developed by Kay Wenger, LMFT, LPCC, and Laguna Beach Counseling, built on exactly that difference."
  - "Why sand? Because it is honest material. It cooperates right up until it does not, it holds a shape for a while, and the ocean always gets a vote. Children use sand, imagination, storytelling, and therapeutic play to build something real, and while they build it they are building other things too: emotional resilience, coping skills, confidence, communication, and stronger relationships at home. Very little of it feels like an appointment, which is rather the point."
