  <h2>Who it helps</h2>
  <p>Sand Castle Therapy suits a lot of what brings children in: <a href="/specialties/anxiety">anxiety</a> and social anxiety, school avoidance, a divorce at home, ADHD and other <a href="/specialties/neurodiversity">ways of being wired</a>, <a href="/specialties/grief">grief</a>, <a href="/specialties/depression">depression</a>, shaky self-esteem, and the daily work of emotional regulation. If your child's version of hard is not on that list, it is still worth a call. We will tell you honestly whether this is the right fit, or whether indoor sessions, family work, or something else altogether makes more sense.</p>
  <p>Sessions are led by Rozy, AMFT, one of the associate therapists Kay personally supervises and the children specialist here. They run after school and on weekends, because a model built around a child's real life ought to fit a family's real calendar. And when the coast is not cooperating, we move indoors, so nobody loses their week to the weather.</p>
{% endcall %}
